docs/CURRENT_STATE.md:36:## Next task: isolated end-to-end concurrency comparison (D173)
docs/CURRENT_STATE.md:40:D172's opt-in coordinator preserves current-prefix requests, ordered writes and dependency-ordered daily judging. Its offline checks cover stale requests, shared identical Jev calls, failure and restart. The default replay remains serial; group ownership and product semantics have not changed.
docs/CURRENT_STATE.md:42:D173 completed the [isolated live API smoke](../poc/reports/2026-10-25-api-smoke/results.md): 36 valid requests, no automatic retries, and all 122 existing database files unchanged. Three two-request samples measured median ratios of 1.08x for extraction and 1.77x for Jev, with individual concurrent samples slower than controls. The Standard list-price estimate was $0.041837; conservative usage accounting was $0.127629 under a $1.50 cap. This uses concurrent ordinary endpoints, not the asynchronous OpenAI Batch API. The full suite passed 152 tests; five accounting/failure mutants were caught.
docs/DECISIONS.md:2088:## D142 · 2026-10-24 · Test organization inside ingestion, not after extraction
docs/DECISIONS.md:2090:- Alex corrected the research direction: thesis associations should emerge during extraction and streaming ingestion. He authorized a short original-article replay through extraction, matching and writing, with no separate full-library clustering pass.
docs/DECISIONS.md:2091:- The isolated POC uses three original articles, three independent samples and ordinary-ingestion controls. New grouping fields are part of existing extraction/matching calls; original checks and writer are reused. No sealed database, production prompt, MCP or UI changes.
docs/DECISIONS.md:2093:- The experiment's affected-group bookkeeping defect was fixed and verified by replaying all 37 identical requests without network calls. Findings: `docs/research/2026-10-24-ingestion-groups/findings.md`.
docs/DECISIONS.md:2095:## D143 · 2026-10-24 · Test one owner for ingestion relationships
docs/DECISIONS.md:2103:## D144 · 2026-10-25 · Research continuing subject identity inside ingestion
docs/DECISIONS.md:2107:- Keep the three original articles, three fresh paired samples against D143, the same model/settings, and the existing maximum of 48 calls/$8 estimated. If the three new core grouping samples pass, use one predetermined additional Rubin customer-deployment article per new stream (as late arrival) to test another milestone; no new comparison claim. Full contract, prior decisions, research sources and fixed criteria: `docs/research/2026-10-25-ingestion-threads/plan.md`.
docs/DECISIONS.md:2110:- A zero-call diagnostic changed only those six self-targets to the required empty new-target representation; both first articles then wrote three theses and three threads. This isolates a format-boundary failure, not successful automatic grouping. No production adoption. A proposal to replace local pointer chains with direct identity groups remains unimplemented and needs a revised experiment contract. Findings: `docs/research/2026-10-25-ingestion-threads/findings.md`.
docs/DECISIONS.md:2270:## D159 · 2026-10-25 · 从抽取到入库重放，先修读取顺序，单独检验身份所需来源
docs/DECISIONS.md:2280:- Alex 同意 D159 的界限并要求继续完整修复。以同一可核对问题判去重，以同一业务过程判归组；拟议担保改成当年实际付款属于抽取失真，不能强行合并算修复。
docs/DECISIONS.md:2307:- Alex selected a fresh English library: “yes start an english library work. how was this lib constructed previously, and how should we do it noe”. Start from original sources and an empty, separately named ledger; preserve the old Chinese ledgers and their raw answers. Do not copy translated thesis rows or append English ingestion to the old library. The [build plan](research/2026-10-25-english/english-library.md) records the old construction, selected source population and staged verification. This selection does not promote D162, enable default grouping, or authorize a larger spending cap.
docs/DECISIONS.md:2364:- Recommendation awaiting Alex's choice: concurrent request preparation with exact read validation before sequential commits, retaining D149/D159 semantics; re-run requests whose inputs changed. A more aggressive day-start extraction contract must be decided and tested separately. The review defines both boundaries, failure/recovery states, local-ID namespacing, evaluation limits and staged tests.
docs/DECISIONS.md:2368:## D172 · 2026-10-25 · Build the isolated ordered-concurrency POC
docs/DECISIONS.md:2371:- Speculative calls may precede earlier commits in the experimental path; accepted handovers and writes may not. Stale prepared requests are recomputed; earlier failure cancels pending work and drains running calls without accepting later results. This scheduling distinction is explicit, not an accidental weakening of D159.
docs/DECISIONS.md:2373:- Offline slice result: [ordered-concurrency POC](../poc/reports/2026-10-25-concurrency-poc/results.md). Shared request identity prevents conflicting concurrent answers under one archive ID. Bounded Jev submission cancels pending work on failure; the daily cost log includes discarded speculative work. Default replay remains serial. 143 tests pass; five intended mutants fail; 3,595 historical request hashes are unchanged. Final focused review finds no serious issue. Live accounting, fresh controls and speed measurement remain outstanding; no paid ingestion calls were made.
