One serious finding:

**[P2] The exact-prefix audit does not verify which answer was accepted.** At [ingestion.py:176](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/poc/concurrency_study/ingestion.py:176), it only checks that the rebuilt request exists somewhere in the archive. It never ties that request’s answer to the saved handover.

I reproduced a false pass entirely in memory: a replay using stored answers passed the audit; replacing its first accepted handover—3 evidence items and 1 candidate—with an empty answer still passed, with unchanged “accepted request” hashes.

This means the audit cannot establish the plan’s central guarantee that every accepted extraction used its actual committed prefix. Each handover needs a verified link to its accepted call and rebuilt request.

